---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import casinos from '../../data/casinos.json';
const lastUpdated = 'August 27, 2026';
const verifiedCount = casinos.filter((c) => c.handsOnVerified).length;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Editorial Policy"
  description="How USAPrizes.com researches, rates, and updates its sweepstakes casino reviews and lottery content, and how affiliate relationships work."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <Breadcrumbs items={[{ name: 'Editorial Policy', href: '/editorial-policy/' }]} />
      <h1>Editorial Policy</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

      <h2 id="reviewer">Who reviews this site</h2>
      <p>
        USAPrizes.com is founded, written, and maintained by <strong>Ora</strong>. There's no
        anonymous "expert team" behind the byline &mdash; ratings and rankings reflect one
        person's editorial judgment, made transparently, and are corrected in public when
        they're wrong. Questions or corrections go straight to the address in the
        <a href="#contact">Contact</a> section below.
      </p>

      <h2 id="how-we-review">How we review</h2>
      <p>
        Every casino review starts from cross-checked public research: the operator's own
        published terms, plus independent reporting, compared across multiple sources rather
        than taken from any single listing. We evaluate each operator on:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Redemption speed and reliability</li>
        <li>Payment and redemption methods offered</li>
        <li>Game selection and software providers</li>
        <li>State availability and current legal status</li>
        <li>Bonus terms and how clearly they're disclosed</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We're moving each review beyond desk research to genuine hands-on account testing,
        including real redemption attempts, since every sweepstakes casino we cover is free to
        join. That's an ongoing process, not something claimed retroactively: each review states
        plainly whether it's hands-on verified yet or still desk-research-based, and updates as
        testing is completed. Current status: <strong>{verifiedCount} of {casinos.length}</strong>{' '}
        brands hands-on verified.
      </p>
      <p>
        Ratings and rankings reflect our own editorial judgment. They are not paid placements
        &mdash; no operator can buy a higher rating or a spot on our
        <a href="/casinos/best-sweepstakes-casinos/">best sweepstakes casinos</a> page.
      </p>

      <h2>Affiliate relationships</h2>
      <p>
        Some links to sweepstakes casino operators on this site are affiliate links. If you sign
        up through one of those links, we may earn a commission at no additional cost to you.
        This is disclosed on every page where it applies. Affiliate relationships never
        determine whether an operator is reviewed, how it's rated, or whether it appears in our
        rankings.
      </p>

      <h2>Accuracy and updates</h2>
      <p>
        Sweepstakes-casino legality and promotional terms change frequently. We show a visible
        "last updated" date on every review and legality page, and we re-check our top-ranked
        operators on a monthly cadence at minimum. Lottery results are pulled from public state
        data feeds shortly after each drawing; if a discrepancy ever appears, the official state
        lottery result always governs.
      </p>

      <h2 id="contact">Corrections &amp; contact</h2>
      <p>
        If you spot an error &mdash; on a review, a legality page, or anywhere else &mdash;
        email <a href="mailto:hello@usaprizes.com">hello@usaprizes.com</a> and we will
        investigate and correct it promptly. This is also the address for press inquiries and
        general questions.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
